module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.IdealTorsionFree
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.InvertibleTrivialization.Sheaf
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Limits
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Constructions.EpiMono
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute
import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ULiftUnit

/-!
# Ideal sheaves locally generated by a nonzerodivisor

Let `(X, O_X)` be a ringed space and let `I ⊆ O_X` be a sheaf of ideals. Stacks 0GT3 compares

1. `I` is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor: every point has an open neighbourhood `U`
   carrying a section `f ∈ I(U)` with `I|_U = O_U · f` and with multiplication by `f` injective
   on `O_U`;
2. `I` is invertible as an `O_X`-module.

Condition (1) implies condition (2) on every ringed space. The converse holds under the
additional hypothesis that every stalk `O_{X,x}` is a local ring, and that hypothesis cannot be
dropped: on a general ringed space an invertible module need not be locally free of rank one.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular`: condition (1), phrased with the vocabulary
  of `StacksFrontier/Algebra/Category/ModuleCat/Sheaf/IdealTorsionFree.lean`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular` and
  `Stacks.IdealTorsion.isInvertible_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`: condition (1) implies
  condition (2), on an arbitrary ringed space.
* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.isLocallyGeneratedByRegular_of_isInvertible`: condition (2) implies
  condition (1) when every stalk of the structure sheaf is a local ring.
* `Stacks.IdealTorsion.isLocallyGeneratedByRegular_iff_isInvertible`: the two conditions are
  equivalent on a ringed space whose stalks are local rings.

## Implementation notes

The two conditions meet at one sectionwise statement: that multiplication
`c ↦ c · f|_V : O_X(V) → I(V)` is bijective for every open `V` inside the neighbourhood. Its
surjectivity is `Stacks.IdealTorsion.GeneratesIdealOn` verbatim, and its injectivity is
interchangeable with `Stacks.IdealTorsion.IsGeneratorRegularOn` for the structure sheaf: a
relation `f · c = 0` in `O_X(V)` is the image under `i` of the relation `c · f = 0` in `I(V)`,
and `i` is injective on sections because it is a monomorphism. The passage from `c · f = 0` to
`f · c = 0` needs no injectivity, which is why condition (1) implies condition (2) with no
hypothesis on `i` beyond its existence.

Both halves of Stacks 0B8M are available at exactly that sectionwise form:
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isoUnitOver` consumes the bijectivity to produce an isomorphism
`I|_U ≅ O_U` of sheaves of modules on the slice site, and
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_bijective_smul_of_isInvertible` produces the bijectivity from
invertibility. The local-stalk hypothesis enters only through the second, so the asymmetry of
0GT3 is the asymmetry of 0B8M, and nothing is assumed about the stalks in the forward direction.

The ideal sheaf is a monomorphism `i : I ⟶ O_X`, as in `IdealTorsionFree.lean`. Injectivity of
`i` on sections comes from `Mono i` through preservation of finite limits by evaluation at an
open, and is used only for the converse: the forward implication reads the generator through `i`
but never inverts it.

Two spellings are named rather than written out. The restriction of the generator lands in the
restricted-scalars module of `I(V)`, whose scalar action is not the one `map_smul` is stated for,
so `resGen` records it at `I(V)` itself; and the sections of the structure sheaf viewed as a
module over itself are the sections of the structure sheaf, but not syntactically, so
`genSection` records the image of the generator at the latter, where multiplication is available
and commutative. Each argument then runs in a single ring.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT3)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0B8M](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0B8M)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0GT5](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GT5)
-/

@[expose] public section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits TopologicalSpace Opposite
open Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorStalkRingedSpace (O ringStalk)

universe u

namespace Stacks.IdealTorsion

variable (X : RingedSpace.{u})

local notation "Oₓ" => structureSheafRing X
local notation "𝒪" => SheafOfModules.unit Oₓ

/-- The ideal sheaf `I` is locally generated by a nonzerodivisor: every point of `X` has an open
neighbourhood `U` and a section `f ∈ I(U)` generating `I|_U` whose multiplication on the
structure sheaf is injective. This is condition (1) of Stacks 0GT3. -/
public def IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, ∃ (U : Opens X) (_ : x ∈ U) (f : I.val.obj (op U)),
    GeneratesIdealOn X U f ∧ IsGeneratorRegularOn X i 𝒪 U f

/-- The restriction of a section of the ideal to a smaller open, recorded at the module of
sections over that open. -/
private noncomputable def resGen {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} {U : Opens X} (V : Opens X)
    (hVU : V ≤ U) (f : I.val.obj (op U)) : I.val.obj (op V) :=
  (I.val.map (homOfLE hVU).op).hom f

/-- The section of the structure sheaf underlying the restriction of a section of the ideal. -/
private noncomputable def genSection {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) {U : Opens X}
    (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U) (f : I.val.obj (op U)) : (O X).obj (op V) :=
  (i.val.app (op V)).hom (resGen X V hVU f)

/-- Regularity of a local generator, read as cancellation in the ring of sections of the
structure sheaf. -/
private lemma eq_zero_of_isGeneratorRegularOn {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪)
    {U : Opens X} {f : I.val.obj (op U)} (hreg : IsGeneratorRegularOn X i 𝒪 U f)
    (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U) (c : (O X).obj (op V))
    (hc : c * genSection X i V hVU f = 0) : c = 0 := by
  refine hreg V hVU (a₁ := c) (a₂ := 0) ?_
  simp only [smul_zero]
  change genSection X i V hVU f * c = 0
  exact (mul_comm _ _).trans hc

/-- The image under `i` of a multiple of the restricted generator is the product in the ring of
sections with `genSection`. -/
private lemma app_smul_resGen {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) {U : Opens X}
    (f : I.val.obj (op U)) (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U) (c : (O X).obj (op V)) :
    (i.val.app (op V)).hom (c • resGen X V hVU f) = c * genSection X i V hVU f :=
  map_smul _ _ _

/-- Multiplication by a local generator which is a nonzerodivisor is a bijection
`O_X(V) → I(V)` for every smaller open `V`. Surjectivity is generation; injectivity reads the
relation `c · f = 0` through `i`, where regularity applies. -/
private lemma bijective_smul_of_generatesIdealOn {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪)
    (U : Opens X) (f : I.val.obj (op U)) (hgen : GeneratesIdealOn X U f)
    (hreg : IsGeneratorRegularOn X i 𝒪 U f) (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U) :
    Function.Bijective fun c : X.presheaf.obj (op V) => c • resGen X V hVU f := by
  constructor
  · intro c₁ c₂ hc
    refine sub_eq_zero.1 (eq_zero_of_isGeneratorRegularOn X i hreg V hVU (c₁ - c₂) ?_)
    rw [← app_smul_resGen, sub_smul, show c₁ • resGen X V hVU f = c₂ • resGen X V hVU f from hc,
      sub_self]
    exact map_zero _
  · exact fun a => (hgen V hVU a).imp fun _ => Eq.symm

/-- A section whose multiplication `c ↦ c · f|_V` is bijective over every smaller open generates
the ideal there. -/
private lemma generatesIdealOn_of_bijective_smul {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ}
    (U : Opens X) (f : I.val.obj (op U))
    (hbij : ∀ (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U),
      Function.Bijective fun c : X.presheaf.obj (op V) => c • resGen X V hVU f) :
    GeneratesIdealOn X U f :=
  fun V hVU a => ((hbij V hVU).2 a).imp fun _ => Eq.symm

/-- Cancellation in the ring of sections against the image of a section whose multiplication is
bijective: a relation `c · f = 0` downstairs is the image of `c · f = 0` upstairs, and `i` is
injective on sections. -/
private lemma eq_zero_of_bijective_smul {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) [Mono i]
    {U : Opens X} (f : I.val.obj (op U)) (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U)
    (hbij : Function.Bijective fun c : X.presheaf.obj (op V) => c • resGen X V hVU f)
    (c : (O X).obj (op V)) (hc : c * genSection X i V hVU f = 0) : c = 0 := by
  have h2 : c • resGen X V hVU f = 0 :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.injective_app_of_mono i (op V)
      ((app_smul_resGen X i f V hVU c).trans (hc.trans (map_zero _).symm))
  exact hbij.1 (a₁ := c) (a₂ := 0) (by simpa only [zero_smul] using h2)

/-- A section whose multiplication `c ↦ c · f|_V` is bijective over every smaller open is a
nonzerodivisor on the structure sheaf there. -/
private lemma isGeneratorRegularOn_of_bijective_smul {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪)
    [Mono i] (U : Opens X) (f : I.val.obj (op U))
    (hbij : ∀ (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U),
      Function.Bijective fun c : X.presheaf.obj (op V) => c • resGen X V hVU f) :
    IsGeneratorRegularOn X i 𝒪 U f := by
  intro V hVU
  change Function.Injective fun c : (O X).obj (op V) => genSection X i V hVU f * c
  intro c₁ c₂ hc
  refine sub_eq_zero.1 (eq_zero_of_bijective_smul X i f V hVU (hbij V hVU) (c₁ - c₂) ?_)
  rw [mul_comm, mul_sub]
  exact sub_eq_zero.2 hc

/-- An ideal sheaf locally generated by a nonzerodivisor is trivial on a neighbourhood of every
point: multiplication by the generator is an isomorphism `O_V ≅ I|_V` over each smaller open, and
those neighbourhoods cover the space. -/
private lemma exists_cover_isoUnit {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪)
    (h : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X i) :
    ∃ W : X.carrier → Opens X, (Opens.grothendieckTopology X).CoversTop W ∧
      ∀ x, Nonempty (I.over (W x) ≅ SheafOfModules.unit ((Oₓ).over (W x))) := by
  choose U hxU f hgen hreg using h
  refine ⟨U, ?_, fun x => ⟨Stacks.SheafOfModules.isoUnitOver I (U x) (f x)
    (bijective_smul_of_generatesIdealOn X i (U x) (f x) (hgen x) (hreg x))⟩⟩
  refine (Opens.coversTop_iff _ U).2 (IsOpenCover.mk ?_)
  ext y
  simpa using ⟨y, hxU y⟩

/-- **Condition (1) of Stacks 0GT3 implies finite local freeness of rank one.** An ideal sheaf
locally generated by a nonzerodivisor is finite locally free of rank one on every ringed space:
a local generator which is a nonzerodivisor trivializes the ideal on its neighbourhood, and
those neighbourhoods cover the space. -/
public theorem isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular
    {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) (h : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X i) :
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.IsFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
      (C := Opens X) (J := Opens.grothendieckTopology X) I 1 := by
  obtain ⟨W, hW, φ⟩ := exists_cover_isoUnit X i h
  have htriv : Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.IsLocallyTrivial I := ⟨X.carrier, W, hW, φ⟩
  exact
    (Stacks.InvertibleLocallyFree.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_iff_invertible_isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank
      X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X).property I 1).2
    (Stacks.SheafOfModules.Invertible.isFiniteLocallyFreeOfRank_one_of_isLocallyTrivial I)

/-- **Condition (1) of Stacks 0GT3 implies condition (2).** An ideal sheaf locally generated by
a nonzerodivisor is invertible as an `O_X`-module. There is no hypothesis on the stalks of the
structure sheaf: this half of the tag holds on every ringed space. -/
@[stacks 0GT3 "(1) implies (2)"]
public theorem isInvertible_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular
    {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) (h : IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X i) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X).property I :=
  have ⟨_W, hW, φ⟩ := exists_cover_isoUnit X i h
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.isInvertible_of_coversTop_nonempty_iso_unit X.presheaf
    (structureSheafRing X).property I hW φ

/-- **Condition (2) of Stacks 0GT3 implies condition (1) when the stalks are local rings.** An
invertible ideal sheaf on a ringed space all of whose stalks `O_{X,x}` are local rings is
locally generated by a nonzerodivisor. The hypothesis on the stalks is the one the tag requires
and cannot be dropped: without it an invertible module need not be locally free of rank one. -/
@[stacks 0GT3 "(2) implies (1) when the stalks are local rings"]
public theorem isLocallyGeneratedByRegular_of_isInvertible
    [∀ x : X.carrier, IsLocalRing (ringStalk X x)]
    {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) [Mono i]
    (h : Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X).property I) :
    IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X i := by
  have := h
  intro x
  obtain ⟨U, hxU, f, hbij⟩ :=
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_bijective_smul_of_isInvertible (X := X) I x
  have hbij' : ∀ (V : Opens X) (hVU : V ≤ U),
      Function.Bijective fun c : X.presheaf.obj (op V) => c • resGen X V hVU f := hbij
  exact ⟨U, hxU, f, generatesIdealOn_of_bijective_smul X U f hbij',
    isGeneratorRegularOn_of_bijective_smul X i U f hbij'⟩

/-- **Stacks 0GT3 on a ringed space whose stalks are local rings.** An ideal sheaf is locally
generated by a nonzerodivisor exactly when it is invertible as an `O_X`-module. Only the
implication from invertibility consumes the hypothesis on the stalks; the other is
`isInvertible_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular`, which holds on every ringed space. -/
public theorem isLocallyGeneratedByRegular_iff_isInvertible
    [∀ x : X.carrier, IsLocalRing (ringStalk X x)]
    {I : SheafOfModules.{u} Oₓ} (i : I ⟶ 𝒪) [Mono i] :
    IsLocallyGeneratedByRegular X i ↔
      Stacks.SheafOfModules.IsInvertible X.presheaf (structureSheafRing X).property I :=
  ⟨isInvertible_of_isLocallyGeneratedByRegular X i,
    isLocallyGeneratedByRegular_of_isInvertible X i⟩

end Stacks.IdealTorsion

end
